Explanation and Advice for the Reported ALERTS
================================================================================

================================================================================
ALERT_005 Type_5 Informative Message, Check.
================================================================================
 No embedded 'refinement details' records were found in the CIF. Acta Cryst.
 requires the inclusion of the last shelxl.res file (in case of a SHELXL or
 XL refinement or similar for non-SHELXL refinement programs) in the CIF,
 embedded between records with semicolons in position 1, preceded by an
 '_iucr_refine_instructions_details' record.
 Note: SHELXL20xy will automatically include the final .res as an embedded
 comment with the dataname '_shelx_res_file'.

================================================================================
ALERT_007 Type_5 Informative Message, Check.
================================================================================
 It is standard practice to refine Hydrogen atoms on hetero atoms as proof of
 their correct assignment.

================================================================================
ALERT_008 Type_5 Informative Message, Check.
================================================================================
 No reflection records were found in the CIF. Acta Cryst. and 'FAIR' require
 the inclusion of the unmerged reflection file used in the final refinement
 (shelxl.hkl in case of a SHELXL or XL refinement) in the CIF, embedded
 between records with semicolons in position 1 and preceded by an
 '_iucr_refine_instructions_details' record.
 Note: SHELXL20xy will automatically include the .hkl as an embedded
 comment with the dataname '_shelx_hkl_file'.

================================================================================
ALERT_010 Type_1 CIF Construction/Syntax Error, Inconsistent or Missing Data.
================================================================================
 Validation is not complete without the availability of the diffraction data.
 Deposited reflection data are preferably the set of reflections that were
 used in the final refinement and embedded in the CIF between records with
 semicolons in position 1 and preceded by an _iucr_refine_reflections_details
 record.  SHELXL20xy will do that automatically. Alternatively, an external
 file with final observed, calculated and sigma reflection data will be the
 minimum for validation and archival.

================================================================================
ALERT_025 Type_1 CIF Construction/Syntax Error, Inconsistent or Missing Data.
================================================================================
 Check reported h,k,l - range with calculated range based on reported
 theta-max.

================================================================================
ALERT_048 Type_1 CIF Construction/Syntax Error, Inconsistent or Missing Data.
================================================================================
 The Moiety formula (i.e. the specification of the various species in the
 structure) should be given in the CIF.

 Example: '(Cd 2+)3, (C6 N6Cr 3-)2, 2(H2 O)'

================================================================================
ALERT_050 Type_1 CIF Construction/Syntax Error, Inconsistent or Missing Data.
================================================================================
 The linear absorption coefficient corresponding to the Sumformula should be
 given.

================================================================================
ALERT_081 Type_1 CIF Construction/Syntax Error, Inconsistent or Missing Data.
================================================================================
 A maximum shift/error should be specified in order to judge convergence.

================================================================================
ALERT_152 Type_1 CIF Construction/Syntax Error, Inconsistent or Missing Data.
================================================================================
 Some software packages calculate Volume s.u.'s incorrectly. The correct
 formula  for triclinic, monoclinic and orthorhombic systems
 (based on the propagation of error expression) may be found in:

 M. Nardelli, Computer & Chemistry, (1983), 7, 95-98.
 or
 C. Giacovazzo ed. in 'Fundamentals of Crystallography', Second Edition,
 Oxford University Press, 2003,  p135.

 Also note that several cell parameters for higher symmetry cells are no
 longer independent. S.u. calculations need special treatment in those cases.

================================================================================
ALERT_183 Type_1 CIF Construction/Syntax Error, Inconsistent or Missing Data.
================================================================================
 Please supply the value for _cell_measurement_reflns_used.

================================================================================
ALERT_184 Type_1 CIF Construction/Syntax Error, Inconsistent or Missing Data.
================================================================================
 Please supply the value for _cell_measurement_theta_min.

================================================================================
ALERT_185 Type_1 CIF Construction/Syntax Error, Inconsistent or Missing Data.
================================================================================
 Please supply the value for _cell_measurement_theta_max.

================================================================================
ALERT_699 Type_1 CIF Construction/Syntax Error, Inconsistent or Missing Data.
================================================================================
 Examples of expected values are 'block', 'needle', 'plate', 'sphere',
 'cylinder'. In case of 'cylinder' or 'sphere' also provide a value for
 '_exptl_size_rad'.

================================================================================
ALERT_720 Type_4 Improvement, Methodology, Query or Suggestion.
================================================================================
 Up to 4 Character Labels of the type C11, H101, N10A, i.e. chemical symbol +
 number + optional letter are to be preferred.
 Note: SHELXL based refinements may use labels up to 7 characters (Including
 residue and or disorder information).

================================================================================
ALERT_760 Type_1 CIF Construction/Syntax Error, Inconsistent or Missing Data.
================================================================================
 The CIF contains no torsion angle entries. This might be accomplished with
 the SHELXL instruction CONF.
 Inclusion is encouraged by Acta Cryst. but not necessarily so by other
 journals.

================================================================================
ALERT_761 Type_1 CIF Construction/Syntax Error, Inconsistent or Missing Data.
================================================================================
 The CIF contains no X-H Bonds. This might be caused by not using the
 SHELXL instruction BOND $H. Inclusion is required by Acta Cryst. but not
 necessarily so by other journals.

